  "notes": "Boot an NBA S.A.M. ROM from an empty NVRAM with four balls on trough switches 18-21, insert four coins and press Start, let the team-selection screen time out and model one served and plunged ball, then hit each pop bumper switch (30, 31, 32) and each slingshot switch (26, 27) once, 2.5 s apart, in two passes of opposite order. Each hit is a short host pulse; the observation is which public solenoid the ROM fires in response, which pairs every bumper and slingshot switch with its coil. The scenario names no driver.",
